# Text comparison

Unified output (the default when stdout is not a terminal). Exit status 1 means
"differences found".

```console
$ mydiff a.txt b.txt
? 1
--- a.txt
+++ b.txt
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 alpha
-beta
 gamma
-delta
+delta changed
+zeta
 epsilon

```

Identical inputs print nothing and exit 0.

```console
$ mydiff a.txt a.txt

```

Side-by-side, summary and quiet modes.

```console
$ mydiff --format side-by-side a.txt b.txt
? 1
     a.txt                                    b.txt
   1 alpha                                  1 alpha
   2 beta                              -
   3 gamma                                  2 gamma
   4 delta                             ~    3 delta changed
                                       +    4 zeta
   5 epsilon                                5 epsilon

$ mydiff -f summary a.txt b.txt
? 1
a.txt vs b.txt: 1 removed, 1 added, 1 modified (3 equal)

$ mydiff -q a.txt b.txt
? 1

```

Whitespace knobs: exact (default), trailing, all.

```console
$ mydiff -f summary ws1.c ws2.c
? 1
ws1.c vs ws2.c: 0 removed, 0 added, 2 modified (1 equal)

$ mydiff -f summary -Z ws1.c ws2.c
? 1
ws1.c vs ws2.c: 0 removed, 0 added, 1 modified (2 equal)

$ mydiff -w ws1.c ws2.c

```

Whitelist + mask: only compare ERROR lines, with timestamps masked.

```console
$ mydiff --only ' ERROR ' --mask '^\S+ \S+=>T' run1.log run2.log

```

Comparing a file with a directory uses the same file name inside it.

```console
$ mydiff -f summary a.txt dir
? 1
a.txt vs dir/a.txt: 1 removed, 1 added, 1 modified (3 equal)

```

JSON output for scripts.

```console
$ mydiff -f json -Z ws1.c ws2.c
? 1
{
  "mode": "text",
  "left": "ws1.c",
  "right": "ws2.c",
  "identical": false,
  "stats": {
    "equal": 2,
    "removed": 0,
    "added": 0,
    "modified": 1,
    "ignored": 0
  },
  "rows": [
    {
      "kind": "modified",
      "left": {
        "number": 1,
        "text": "if (x) {",
        "changed": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 3
          },
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 7
          }
        ]
      },
      "right": {
        "number": 1,
        "text": "if(x){"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "equal",
      "left": {
        "number": 2,
        "text": "  y();  "
      },
      "right": {
        "number": 2,
        "text": "  y();"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "equal",
      "left": {
        "number": 3,
        "text": "}"
      },
      "right": {
        "number": 3,
        "text": "}"
      }
    }
  ]
}

```
